      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:1:39:6",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا بَلَغَ الْغُلَامُ ثَلَاثَ عَشْرَةَ سَنَةً كُتِبَتْ لَهُ الْحَسَنَةُ وَ كُتِبَتْ عَلَيْهِ السَّيِّئَةُ وَ عُوقِبَ وَ إِذَا بَلَغَتِ الْجَارِيَةُ تِسْعَ سِنِينَ فَكَذَلِكَ وَ ذَلِكَ أَنَّهَا تَحِيضُ لِتِسْعِ سِنِينَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from Al Hassan, from Ja’far Bin Sama’at, from Adam Baya Al Lulu, from Abdullah Bin Sinan, ",
          "Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> has said: ‘When the boy reaches thirteen years, the good deeds are Written for him, and the evil deeds are Written against him, and Punished. And when the girl reaches nine years, so it is like that, and that is because she menstruates at nine years’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. It is narrated from the narrator of the previous Hadith from al-Hassan from Ja‘far ibn Sama‘ah from Adam, Bayya’ al-Lu’lu from ‘Abd Allah ibn Sinan who has narrated the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘When a boy become thirteen years old his doing good deeds are written for him as well as bad deeds for which he will be punished. When a girl becomes nine years old it also is the same because she experiences Hayd (menses) when she is nine years old.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
